# Before you answer

Check the plan against the brief:
- Every number and item from the key messages is in exactly one component, copied exactly; nothing is added; the kicker, headline and subtitle appear only in the header.
- No item, line or label appears twice: not across components, not on every card, not as a restatement of the headline, subtitle or visual direction.
- Each structure is drawn at the level the brief fills it; order is shown only where the brief has it.
- Every named step is its own node; no chart series mixes units.
- Each diagram's direction fits its band and its count fits that place.
- At most one hero; the focus, if any, is what the headline names.
- Every component, the title included, has a design_hint that names a treatment; on a cover or section_break the title is the hero.
